Q: Codeigniter Selecting Data using CURDATE() A: <p>I think you need to format the datetime column as a date to compare against the current date. Because your comparing datetime with date, there can never be a match. You need to extract the date from <code>adate</code> using MySQL's <code>DATE_FORMAT()</code> function  <code>DATE_FORMAT(adate,&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)</code>.</p>
<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('DATE_FORMAT(adate,&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)', 'CURDATE()', false);
</code></pre>

Q: append on useFieldArray A: <p>When you're register the input field, you're essentially also giving it a name. In this case its names &quot;values&quot;. The reason the append is not working, is because it's not provided what to append. You have to provide it the name of the input field.</p>
<p>This is your register:  {...register(<code>values.${index}</code>, {
required: &quot;This field is required&quot;
})}
So this should be your append: append({ values: &quot;&quot; });</p>
<p>codesand box: <a href="https://codesandbox.io/s/bold-https-4j281f?file=/src/App.js:1343-1365" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codesandbox.io/s/bold-https-4j281f?file=/src/App.js:1343-1365</a></p>

